  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Celebrating 16-days of activism against gender-based violence in Katutura and Okahandja.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the project is to celebrate the 16-days of activism against Gender-Based Violence in three communities, in order to encourage community members to reflect on the issue and ensure they know (in particular girls and women) who to contact should they face violence at home. 
Key beneficiaries will be 2,400 community members from two areas in Katutura, Windhoek and one area in the main location of Okahandja, of which 60% (1,560) are women and girls. 
Through interactive activities with the community dance troupe, our photo exhibition &#x2018;the caring Namibian man&#x2019;, clips and films, the audience will be encouraged to reflect on what happens in their location, share ideas on how they can become agents for change, ensure there&#x2019;s zero tolerance for gender-based violence in their area and commit to do better during this festive season.</narrative>
  </description>
